<title>UK: Yorkshire spurts up after recent buyback.</title>
<headline>Yorkshire spurts up after recent buyback.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Yorkshire Water Plc shot 22p, or six percent, higher to 388-1/2p by 0905 GMT in further reaction to the company's share buyback operations on Monday, dealers said.</p>
<p>&quot;The yield in some of these utilities look quite attractive at the moment. The buy-back on Monday has been known about for a long time but has once again focused attention on the sector,&quot; the head of trading at a large brokerage said.</p>
<p>On Monday broker SBC Warburg executed a share buyback plan for Yorkshire, representing 89 percent of the B shares in issue. All the repurchased shares will be cancelled.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
